[{ "action": "append", "id": "event-modals", "value" : "<div tabindex=\"-1\" id=\"modal-4b03d06c-ec0b-47ed-8140-253086bbac80\" class=\"modal\"><div class=\"modal-dialog modal-lg\"><div class=\"modal-content\"><div class=\"modal-header\"><a data-dismiss=\"modal\" class=\"close\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-remove\"></span></a><p class=\"text-muted\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-road\"></span> Research Papers</p><strong>Thu 9 Jul 2026 14:20 - 14:40 at <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/room/fse-2026/fse-2026-venue-mb-5.215\" class=\"room-link navigate\">MB 5.215</a></strong> - <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/track/fse-2026/fse-2026-research-papers#program\" class=\"navigate\">Anomaly and failure 2</a> <small>Chair(s): <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/fse-2026/domenicobianculli\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\">Domenico Bianculli</a></small></div><div class=\"modal-body\"><div class=\"bg-primary event-title\"><h4><span data-event-star=\"4b03d06c-ec0b-47ed-8140-253086bbac80\" title=\"Add event to your program\"><span class=\"text-disabled glyphicon glyphicon-star-empty\"></span></span><strong>Spectrum-based Failure Attribution for Multi-Agent Systems</strong></h4></div><div class=\"bg-info event-description\"><p>Large Language Model Powered Multi-Agent Systems (MASs) are increasingly employed to automate complex real-world problems, such as programming and scientific discovery. Despite their promising, MASs are not without their flaws. However, failure attribution in MASs\u2014pinpointing the specific agent actions responsible for failures\u2014remains underexplored and labor-intensive, posing significant challenges for debugging and system improvement. To bridge this gap, we propose FAMAS, the first spectrum-based failure attribution approach for MASs, which operates through systematic trajectory replay and abstraction, followed by spectrum analysis. The core idea of FAMAS is to estimate, from variations across repeated MAS executions, the likelihood that each agent action is responsible for the failure. In particular, we propose a novel suspiciousness formula tailored to MASs, which integrates two key factor groups, namely the agent behavior group and the action behavior group, to account for the agent activation patterns and the action activation patterns within the execution trajectories of MASs. Through expensive evaluations against 12 baselines on the Who&amp;When benchmark, FAMAS demonstrates superior performance by outperforming all the methods in comparison.</p>\n<p></p><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.13782\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"publication-link navigate\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-link\"></span> Pre-print</a><p></p><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/fse-2026/yuge\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Yu Ge<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Nanjing University</span></h5></div></div></a></div><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/fse-2026/linnaxie\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Linna Xie<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Nanjing University</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>China</small></h5></div></div></a></div></div><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/fse-2026/zhongli4\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"Zhong Li\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getProfileImage/zhongli4/57e42384-effc-42a5-82de-69ebdb9f3e1d/micro-avatar?1784966713000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Zhong Li<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Nanjing University</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>China</small></h5></div></div></a></div><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/fse-2026/yupei\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"Yu Pei\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getProfileImage/yupei/7b7cf284-c81a-473b-9647-f0794252b028/micro-avatar?1784966714000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Yu Pei<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Hong Kong Polytechnic University</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>China</small></h5></div></div></a></div></div><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/fse-2026/tianzhang\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"Tian Zhang\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getProfileImage/tianzhang/239d897e-c434-4def-bf89-fab0f8ffbe85/micro-avatar?1784966711000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Tian Zhang<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Nanjing University</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>China</small></h5></div></div></a></div></div></div><br>